    <string name="settings_assistant">Kai as your digital assistant</string>
    <string name="assistant_intro">As the digital assistant, Kai opens over whatever you are doing when you press and hold the side button (or the power button, or use the corner swipe), and listens at once. Closing it before your first words ends the call; after them the call goes on in the background. While Kai is the assistant, apps that use the system\'s speech recogniser get none from it (keyboards with a recogniser of their own are not affected).</string>
    <string name="assistant_role">Set Kai as the digital assistant app.</string>
    <string name="assistant_default_apps">Open default apps</string>
    <string name="assistant_role_unavailable">This phone does not offer the digital assistant to apps: the Quick Settings tile and the launcher shortcut start a call instead.</string>
    <string name="assistant_button_samsung">The side button: Settings → Advanced features → Side button → Press and hold → Kai (instead of the power-off menu).</string>
    <string name="assistant_button_lineage">The power button: where Settings offers it (System → Gestures → Press and hold power button → Digital assistant), choose it. Otherwise set it once from a computer with adb: adb shell settings put global power_button_long_press 5</string>
    <string name="assistant_button_pixel">The power button: Settings → System → Gestures → Press and hold power button → Digital assistant.</string>
    <string name="assistant_button_other">The power button\'s or the gesture\'s setting for the digital assistant, where the phone offers one; the corner swipe or the home button\'s long press open Kai too once it is the digital assistant.</string>
    <string name="assistant_power_value">On this phone the power button\'s long press is set to %1$d; the assistant\'s value is %2$d.</string>
    <string name="assistant_power_unreadable">Android does not let Kai read the power button\'s long press setting, so it cannot say what it is set to.</string>
    <string name="assistant_power_unset">The power button\'s long press is at the build\'s default (on LineageOS the power menu).</string>
    <string name="assistant_button_done">The button opens Kai</string>
    <string name="assistant_microphone">Microphone: allow it now, so an invocation listens at once instead of asking.</string>
    <string name="assistant_done">Kai is set up as your digital assistant.</string>
    <string name="assistant_open">Some steps are still open.</string>
    <string name="assistant_without_role">Without the role, the Quick Settings tile \"Talk to Kai\" and the launcher shortcut \"Talk\" start a call too.</string>
